She has been an active member of APA committees, including the Committee on Psychology and AIDS, and was vice chair of the Committee on Women in Psychology. Most recently, she has written a book, Should I Stay or Should I Go, Surviving a Religious, relationship with a narcissist. Welcome, Dr. Romney. Thank you so much for having you. I think a lot of our listeners can relate to being involved in a bad or a toxic relationship, but your book sort of touches on something that surprised me. How do we or should we stay in these relationships? And you know, that seems sort of counterintuitive. I think most people would say if you're in a relationship with someone who is bad for you, you should leave, but you're saying that's not always possible, correct? When I called this book, should I stay or should I go, it would have been so.
她是美国心理学会（APA）委员会的活跃成员，包括心理学与艾滋病委员会，并曾担任女性心理学委员会的副主席。最近，她写了一本书《我该留下还是离开：在与自恋者的关系中生存》。欢迎你，罗姆尼博士。非常感谢你的邀请。我想我们的很多听众都能体会到陷入一段糟糕或有毒关系的感觉，但你的书触及了一些让我惊讶的事情。我们如何或者是否应该留在这些关系中？你知道，这似乎有点违反直觉。我想大多数人会说，如果你和对你不利的人在一起，你应该离开，但你说这并不总是可能的，对吗？当我给这本书起名为《我该留下还是离开》时，这本来会非常……

