easy to just call it go. But the fact of the matter is that relationships aren't that simple, are they? And that I felt as a psychologist I really had to look at it through that compassion and realistic lens that people stay in relationships for lots of reasons. Money, security, fear of being alone, culture, religion, children. I mean, the list goes on and they're all very valid and very important reasons. So while a person is in a toxic relationship and doesn't feel at that point that they can leave, I didn't feel like this. then they should remain a human sacrifice or stay in something that was truly a lost cause, but to really give them honest and actionable solutions for how they might be able to stay in,
容易直接叫它《离开》。但事实是，人际关系并没有那么简单，不是吗？作为一名心理学家，我觉得我必须以一种同情和现实的眼光来看待它，人们留在一段关系中有很多原因。金钱、安全感、害怕孤独、文化、宗教、孩子。我的意思是，名单还在继续，它们都是非常正当且非常重要的理由。所以，当一个人处于一段有毒的关系中，并且觉得在那一刻无法离开时，我不觉得他们就应该成为人类牺牲品，或者留在一段注定失败的关系中，而是要给他们提供诚实且可行的解决方案，让他们知道如何能够留在……

