00:03:17.000 --> 00:04:02.000
People with narcissism are often the most insecure people in the room. and they've established a way of showing themselves as anything but that they often look like the most confident person in the room, but there's an emptiness there. I often say that there are sort of four pillars to narcissism. Lack of empathy, grandiosity, a chronic sense of entitlement, and a chronic need to seek out admiration from other people and invalidation from other people. Those really create the core of that disorder. And then that's coupled with the sort of sort of inability to regulate self-esteem, that sense of always peddling faster to get the regard of other people, and has even been viewed very much as a disorder of attachment, that inability to
自恋者往往是房间里最缺乏安全感的人。他们建立了一种方式来展示自己，表现得一点也不像那样。他们看起来往往是房间里最自信的人，但内心却空虚。我常说自恋有四个支柱：缺乏同理心、自负、长期的权利感，以及长期寻求他人赞美和认可的需求。这些构成了该障碍的核心。再加上那种无法调节自尊的能力，那种为了获得他人尊重而不断“加速”的感觉，它甚至被视为一种依恋障碍，即无法……

