00:05:26.000 --> 00:06:00.000
The one day he went from being a raging beast to a prince. A lot of people have taken that fairy tale and they have injected it into their lives saying, if I love him enough, if I dance around enough, if I'm sweet enough, if I'm pretty enough, if I'm this enough, if I'm that enough, then I will please him and he will go from being a raging beast to a prince. It is never going to be enough. And I think that's the real paradox in the narcissistic relationship. So then the bigger question becomes, what do you do? If you're never going to be enough, one thing you need to do is stop exhausting yourself to try to be so.
有一天，他从狂暴的野兽变成了王子。很多人把那个童话故事注入到他们的生活中，说：如果我足够爱他，如果我跳舞跳得足够多，如果我足够甜美，如果我足够漂亮，如果我足够这样，如果我足够那样，那么我就会取悦他，他就会从狂暴的野兽变成王子。这永远不会足够。我认为这就是自恋关系中真正的悖论。那么更大的问题就变成了：你该怎么办？如果你永远无法做到“足够”，你需要做的第一件事就是停止为了尝试做到“足够”而耗尽自己。

