our compassion, our empathy. And that's how I would operate in therapy when I do it. But I have to say that the changes I see are glacial and the people who most often suffer, even though we may be doing good work in therapy, they'll often very quickly go back to their old habits when they're in their relationships. I think there's a lot of blame being put on technology and the rise of social media for a shift in how couples meet and communities. How do you know when social media is working against you in your quest for finding the right person and when it's beneficial?
